| **AT2: Request Resource**        | The robot sends a message to the storage specifying the required resources.                                       | AND      | Storage facility        | 1                | This action is necessary for the storage system to release the requested resources.                                                                              |
| **AT3: Wait for Retrieval**      | The robot waits at the storage until the resources are retrieved.                                                  | AND      | Storage facility        | 1                | The robot must remain at the storage to receive the resources once the retrieval process is complete.                                                             |
| **AT4: Recharge and Reassign**   | The robot returns to the recharging station and assigns the mission to another robot.                              | OR       | Recharging station      | 1                | This fallback action is triggered if the battery is low during collection (below 10%) to ensure mission continuity.                                                |
| **AT5: Navigate to Destination**  | The robot navigates from its current location to the specified delivery destination.                               | AND      | Requesting agent’s location / designated destination | 1                | Delivery requires the robot to reach the destination to hand over the resources.                                                                                 |
| **AT6: Deliver Resource**        | The robot delivers the collected resource to the destination.                                                    | AND      | Destination             | 1                | This is the primary action in the delivery run that completes the resource transfer.                                                                              |
| **AT7: Return Resource to Checkpoint** | The robot returns the resource to a designated checkpoint if battery is low during delivery.                     | OR       | Checkpoint location     | 1                | This fallback action ensures the resource is not lost if the robot cannot complete the delivery due to battery constraints (below 30%).                           |
| **AT8: Alert and Report**        | The robot triggers an alert and sends a report to the sector manager in case returning the resource to a checkpoint fails. | OR       | Robot’s current location / sector manager’s office | 1                | This fallback action is necessary to inform higher management of delivery failures so that corrective actions can be taken.                                     |

──────────────────────────────
3. Summary of Logical Relationships

Below is an overview of how the goals and tasks are logically related:

• G1 -> G1.1 [AND]  
 Justification: The overall mission (G1) requires that the resource collection phase (G1.1) is completed before delivery can begin.

• G1 -> G1.2 [AND]  
 Justification: Both collection and delivery phases are essential to fulfill the overall mission.

• G1.1 -> G1.1.1 [AND]  
 Justification: The collection phase (G1.1) is decomposed into the “Approach and Request Resource” sub-goal (G1.1.1) which covers the detailed steps for resource retrieval.

• G1.1.1 -> AT1, AT2, AT3 [AND]  
 Justification: The “Approach and Request Resource” goal is sequentially composed of navigating (AT1), requesting (AT2), and waiting for retrieval (AT3).

• G1.1.1 -> AT4 [OR fallback]  
 Justification: If the battery is low (below 10%) during collection, the fallback action “Recharge and Reassign” (AT4) is taken instead of the normal sequence.

• G1.2 -> G1.2.1 [AND]  
 Justification: The delivery phase (G1.2) is executed through one or more delivery runs represented by G1.2.1.

• G1.2.1 -> AT5, AT6 [AND]  
 Justification: Each delivery run (G1.2.1) involves navigating to the destination (AT5) and delivering the resource (AT6).

• G1.2.1 -> AT7, AT8 [OR fallback]  
 Justification: If the robot’s battery is low (below 30%) or if returning the resource to a checkpoint fails, fallback actions (AT7: Return Resource to Checkpoint, and AT8: Alert and Report) are activated to ensure mission integrity.

──────────────────────────────
Conclusion

This goal model captures the hierarchical structure and logical relationships required for a multi‐robot system executing a resource collection and delivery mission. The sequential and fallback (AND/OR) decompositions reflect the mission’s requirement for step‐by‐step execution and contingency handling in the event of low battery or delivery failure.

